See LICENSE for the full text.

**Why GPL-3.0 and not something looser.** It is not a preference. The app is
built on comic-text-detector, which is GPL-3.0. That dependency is not optional:
every detection route uses its `seg` head for the ink mask that Clean paints
with, and `inpaint` skips any region that has no mask. Two of the other
detectors are GPL-3.0 as well. Copyleft was in the foundations before there
was a licence file on top.

**What that does and does not require.** GPL-3.0 asks that anyone you
DISTRIBUTE the program to can also get its source, under the same terms.
It says nothing about price -- selling GPL software has always been allowed --
and it does not reach across a network: a translation request sent to a remote
API is two separate programs talking, not one program linked to another, and
running mangatl as a hosted service is not distribution at all.

NO MODEL FILE IS INSIDE THIS SOFTWARE. Every one of them is downloaded by the
installed app on its first start (or by the person, for a checkout), and
pointed at by a path in the project settings. What is listed below is what
the app knows how to READ.

FOUR OF THEM ARE ALSO MIRRORED on this project's own release page
(`github.com/Lerbernard/MangaTCT/releases/tag/models`), and the app tries the
mirror before the publisher: comic-text-detector (GPL-3.0), AnimeText
(GPL-3.0), the Manga109 segmenter (MIT), and the DB++ COO weights (the
authors' release, MIT repository; see its note below). Each is the exact
file its publisher put out, unchanged, checksummed in `tools/models.json`.
Nothing whose licence is not written down is mirrored - the webtoon balloon
models are fetched from their publisher only.


